## Rules for every agent

1. Never change files in `System/` without showing the user the exact change and getting a yes (the only exception: saving the user's own name and company to `System/Settings.md` when they tell you).
2. Never edit `System/Core/`, `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.agents/`, `AGENTS.md` or `CLAUDE.md`. Bron regenerates them from `System/`.
3. Team members never run as subagents. To hand work to a team member, use a ticket. Subagents are only for helpers.
4. Keep the vault tidy: one-off work in `Projects/`, repeating work in `Routines/`. Machine data lives in `.bron/`.
5. Ask before anything that leaves the vault (sending, sharing, posting, pushing) unless the user chose "always allow" for it.

## Tickets

Work between agents goes through tickets in `Tickets/` (see `System/Core/Manual/tickets.md`).
- To hand work to a team member, use the delegate skill.
- When you were started to work a ticket, report with ticket commands: `.bron/bin/bron ticket status <id> blocked --as <your key> --note "<question>"` to ask, `.bron/bin/bron ticket result <id> --as <your key> --text "<summary>"` when done. Your ticket id is in the task you were given (also in $$BRON_TICKET); your key is your agent name in lower case with hyphens (e.g. cfo).
- If an action is refused or needs approval, don't work around it: mark the ticket blocked with a note starting "Needs your OK:" that names the exact action.

